  "id": "prepulse-inhibition",
  "term": "prepulse inhibition",
  "definition": "Prepulse inhibition is a neurophysiological effect in which a startle response becomes smaller when a weaker stimulus happens shortly before the startling one. It is used as a way to measure sensorimotor gating.",
